#: src/recipe-parameters.md:1
msgid "Recipe Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:3
msgid ""
"Recipes may have parameters. Here recipe `build` has a parameter called "
"`target`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:12
msgid "To pass arguments on the command line, put them after the recipe name:"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:20
msgid ""
"To pass arguments to a dependency, put the dependency in parentheses along "
"with the arguments:"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:23
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"default: (build \"main\")\n"
"\n"
"build target:\n"
"  @echo 'Building {{target}}…'\n"
"  cd {{target}} && make\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:31
msgid "Variables can also be passed as arguments to dependencies:"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:33
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"target := \"main\"\n"
"\n"
"_build version:\n"
"  @echo 'Building {{version}}…'\n"
"  cd {{version}} && make\n"
"\n"
"build: (_build target)\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:43
msgid ""
"A command’s arguments can be passed to a dependency by putting the "
"dependency in parentheses along with the arguments:"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:46
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"build target:\n"
"  @echo \"Building {{target}}…\"\n"
"\n"
"push target: (build target)\n"
"  @echo 'Pushing {{target}}…'\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:54
msgid "Parameters may have default values:"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:64
msgid "Parameters with default values may be omitted:"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:72
msgid "Or supplied:"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:80
msgid ""
"Default values may be arbitrary expressions, but expressions containing the "
"`+`, `&&`, `||`, or `/` operators must be parenthesized:"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:83
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"arch := \"wasm\"\n"
"\n"
"test triple=(arch + \"-unknown-unknown\") input=(arch / \"input.dat\"):\n"
"  ./test {{triple}}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:90
msgid ""
"The last parameter of a recipe may be variadic, indicated with either a `+` "
"or a `*` before the argument name:"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:98
msgid ""
"Variadic parameters prefixed with `+` accept _one or more_ arguments and "
"expand to a string containing those arguments separated by spaces:"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:108
msgid ""
"Variadic parameters prefixed with `*` accept _zero or more_ arguments and "
"expand to a string containing those arguments separated by spaces, or an "
"empty string if no arguments are present:"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:112
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"commit MESSAGE *FLAGS:\n"
"  git commit {{FLAGS}} -m \"{{MESSAGE}}\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:117
msgid ""
"Variadic parameters can be assigned default values. These are overridden by "
"arguments passed on the command line:"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:125
msgid ""
"The number of arguments a variadic parameter accepts may be limited with the "
"`[arg(ARG, min=MIN)]` and `[arg(ARG, max=MAX)]` attributes<sup>1.56.0</sup>, "
"which require lists to be enabled:"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:138
msgid "`min` and `max` also apply to default values."
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:140
msgid ""
"`{{…}}` substitutions may need to be quoted if they contain spaces. For "
"example, if you have the following recipe:"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:143
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"search QUERY:\n"
"  lynx https://www.google.com/?q={{QUERY}}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:148
msgid "And you type:"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:150
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ just search \"cat toupee\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:154
msgid ""
"`just` will run the command `lynx https://www.google.com/?q=cat toupee`, "
"which will get parsed by `sh` as `lynx`, `https://www.google.com/?q=cat`, "
"and `toupee`, and not the intended `lynx` and `https://www.google.com/?q=cat "
"toupee`."
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:158
msgid "You can fix this by adding quotes:"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:160
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"search QUERY:\n"
"  lynx 'https://www.google.com/?q={{QUERY}}'\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:165
msgid ""
"Parameters prefixed with a `$` will be exported as environment variables:"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:172
msgid ""
"Parameters may be constrained to match regular expression patterns using the "
"`[arg(\"name\", pattern=PATTERN)]` attribute<sup>1.45.0</sup>:"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:181
msgid "The value of `pattern` may be a const expression<sup>1.55.0</sup>."
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:183
msgid ""
"A leading `^` and trailing `$` are added to the pattern, so it must match "
"the entire argument value."
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:186
msgid ""
"You may constrain the pattern to a number of alternatives using the `|` "
"operator:"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:195
msgid ""
"Regular expressions are provided by the [Rust `regex` crate](https://docs.rs/"
"regex/latest/regex/). See the [syntax documentation](https://docs.rs/regex/"
"latest/regex/#syntax) for usage examples."
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:200
msgid ""
"Usage information for a recipe may be printed with the `--usage` "
"subcommand<sup>1.46.0</sup>:"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:211
msgid ""
"Help strings may be added to arguments using the `[arg(ARG, help=HELP)]` "
"attribute:"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:213
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"[arg(\"bar\", help=\"hello\")]\n"
"foo bar:\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:218
msgid "The value `help` may be a const expression<sup>1.55.0</sup>."
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:228
msgid "Recipe Flags and Options"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:230
msgid "Recipe parameters are positional by default."
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:232 src/recipe-parameters.md:249
#: src/recipe-parameters.md:282 src/recipe-parameters.md:332
msgid "In this `justfile`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:239
msgid "The parameter `bar` is positional:"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:246
msgid ""
"The `[arg(ARG, long=OPTION)]`<sup>1.46.0</sup> attribute can be used to make "
"a parameter a long option."
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:251
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"[arg(\"bar\", long=\"bar\")]\n"
"foo bar:\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:256
msgid "The parameter `bar` is given with the `--bar` option:"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:263
msgid "Options may also be passed with `--name=value` syntax:"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:270
msgid ""
"The value of `long` may be omitted, in which case the option defaults to the "
"name of the parameter. With the following justfile, `bar` may be passed with "
"`--bar`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:274
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"[arg(\"bar\", long)]\n"
"foo bar:\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:279
msgid ""
"The `[arg(ARG, short=OPTION)]`<sup>1.46.0</sup> attribute can be used to "
"make a parameter a short option."
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:284
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"[arg(\"bar\", short=\"b\")]\n"
"foo bar:\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:289
msgid "The parameter `bar` is given with the `-b` option:"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:296
msgid ""
"The value of `short` may be omitted, in which case the option defaults to "
"the first character of the name of the parameter. With the following "
"justfile, `bar` may be passed with `-b`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:300
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"[arg(\"bar\", short)]\n"
"foo bar:\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:305
msgid ""
"If a parameter has both a long and short option, it may be passed using "
"either."
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:307
msgid ""
"Multiple short options may be combined<sup>1.55.0</sup>, for example `-abc` "
"is equivalent to `-a -b -c`. A short option which takes a value may appear "
"last, for example `-abcd VALUE`."
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:311
msgid ""
"Variadic `*` and `+` parameters may be options, in which case the option is "
"repeatable, with each occurrence contributing one value:"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:325
msgid ""
"As with positional variadic parameters, `+` options must be passed at least "
"once, whereas `*` options may be omitted."
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:328
msgid ""
"The `[arg(ARG, value=VALUE, …)]`<sup>1.46.0</sup> attribute can be used with "
"`long` or `short` to make a parameter a flag which does not take a value. "
"`VALUE` may be an expression<sup>1.54.0</sup>."
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:334
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"[arg(\"bar\", long=\"bar\", value=\"hello\")]\n"
"foo bar:\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:339
msgid ""
"The parameter `bar` is given with the `--bar` option, but does not take a "
"value, and instead takes the value given in the `[arg]` attribute:"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:347
msgid ""
"This is useful for unconditionally requiring a flag like `--force` on "
"dangerous commands."
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:350
msgid "A flag is optional if its parameter has a default:"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:352
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"[arg(\"bar\", long=\"bar\", value=\"hello\")]\n"
"foo bar=\"goodbye\":\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:357
msgid "Causing it to receive the default when not passed in the invocation:"
msgstr ""

#: src/recipe-parameters.md:364
msgid ""
"If `--help` or `-h` is passed to a recipe that does not define that option, "
"the recipe’s help string is printed and execution stops<sup>master</sup>."
msgstr ""
